{"traceId":"f7480f0d9639b26ef95721302ecbac83","spans":{"b16faacd86dd9432":{"spanId":"b16faacd86dd9432","traceId":"f7480f0d9639b26ef95721302ecbac83","parentSpanId":"27e5bf2f565898ac","startTime":1753144188163,"endTime":1753144190327.919,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit futher down the chain of command and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or a designated Director) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Greetings. I am online and ready to begin operations. My first action will be to greet the user, introduce myself and the firm's capabilities, and gather the initial requirements for our first project. I will use a `CLARIFY` call to accomplish this, as per my instructions. This will allow me to understand the user's vision and begin formulating a plan. I will await the user's response before taking further action, such as recruiting subordinate agents.\\n\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself as the Chief of Staff for your AWS development firm and to gather the foundational requirements of your project. Understanding your vision is the first step in building a successful application.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\",\\n        \\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\",\\n        \\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        [],\\n        [\\n            \\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\",\\n            \\\"An internal business application (e.g., dashboard, CRM, data management tool).\\\",\\n            \\\"A data processing pipeline or backend service.\\\",\\n            \\\"A mobile application backend.\\\",\\n            \\\"Other (please specify).\\\"\\n        ],\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The user's requirements are clear. They need a website for their HOA with both public and restricted sections, user authentication for residents, and a simple content management system for news updates that doesn't require technical skills. This project can be logically divided into two main components: the backend infrastructure and the frontend user experience.\\n\\nTo effectively manage the planning of these components, I will recruit two Director-level agents, each specializing in one of these areas. This will ensure that both the technical foundation and the user-facing aspects of the project are given expert attention from the outset.\\n\\nFirst, I will recruit a Director of Backend Engineering to handle the server-side architecture. Second, I will recruit a Director of Frontend & User Experience to design the website and ensure it meets the user's requirement for simplicity and ease of use. Once these agents are in place, I will issue orders for them to begin creating their respective plans.\\n\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires significant backend infrastructure for user authentication (residents-only access), secure storage of sensitive documents, a contact form mechanism, and the logic for a simplified content management system. A dedicated Director is necessary to architect a robust, secure, and scalable backend solution using the appropriate AWS services.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly requested a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate website. A Director focused on Frontend and User Experience is critical to plan the website structure, design an intuitive interface, and ensure the client-side application is accessible and meets the user's non-technical requirements for content updates.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend & User Experience\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vorne (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"With the successful recruitment of the Director of Backend Engineering (Vader, 3) and the Director of Frontend & User Experience (Vorne, 2), the next logical step is to delegate the initial planning phase to them. I will issue specific orders to each Director, outlining their responsibilities and expected deliverables. These initial plans will form the basis of our comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vader. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the backend infrastructure of the HOA website project. The user requires user authentication for residents, secure storage and access for sensitive documents, a contact form, and a simple mechanism for a non-technical user to post news/updates. Your plan should detail the proposed AWS services (e.g., Cognito, S3, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Lambda, SES) and the high-level architecture for implementing these features. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vorne. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the frontend and user experience of the HOA website project. The user has emphasized the need for a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface. Your plan should cover the website structure (sitemap), hosting strategy (e.g., S3 static hosting with CloudFront), and the user flow for both public visitors and authenticated residents. Crucially, your plan must include a design for the non-technical news update process from a user-experience perspective, ensuring it aligns with the backend capabilities. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_FRONTEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_frontend_infra_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a well-architected, cost-efficient, and secure hosting plan (S3 static hosting, CloudFront distribution, TLS certificates, caching rules, error handling, and deployment pipeline) we need a dedicated senior Supervisor-rank specialist who can dive deep into AWS frontend infrastructure best practices while coordinating with backend counterparts.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – Frontend Infrastructure\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is logical and necessary for developing a robust frontend infrastructure plan. A specialist in this area will ensure that the website is secure, performant, and reliable, which aligns perfectly with the overall project goals. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (3) is requesting approval for call ID vader-recruit-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the Chief's order (HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01), I require a supervisor to oversee the planning of the authentication and secure data storage components. This agent will be responsible for devising the architecture for resident authentication using AWS Cognito and the secure storage and access control mechanisms for sensitive documents, likely utilizing S3 and IAM policies. This is a critical and specialized area of the plan.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Identity and Data Security\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vader is a logical and necessary step to address the critical security requirements of the project. The specialization of a supervisor for identity and data security is a prudent decision that directly supports the successful completion of order `HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01`. I approve this action.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_ux_sitemap_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A seasoned Supervisor focused on user-experience and information architecture is required to design a clear sitemap, page layouts, accessibility considerations, and resident/public user flows that meet the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"simple, user-friendly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" mandate and integrate smoothly with Cognito-based auth and backend APIs.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – User Experience & Sitemap\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is well-justified. The user explicitly requested a \\\"simple and user-friendly interface.\\\" Dedicating a Supervisor to User Experience & Sitemap is a direct and effective way to ensure this core requirement is met. This role is essential for planning the website's structure and user flow, which is a key part of the frontend plan I ordered. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (3) is requesting approval for call ID vader-recruit-02 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the Chief's order (HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01), I require a supervisor to plan the application logic and content management backend. This agent's responsibility will be to design the architecture for the contact form functionality (using services like API Gateway, Lambda, and SES) and the simple news/update system for non-technical users (likely an S3-triggered Lambda process). This will ensure the interactive elements of the backend are well-designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is another well-reasoned request from Director Vader. Separating the planning of application logic from identity and security allows for focused expertise on each component of the backend. This supervisor will be essential for designing the interactive parts of the website, such as the contact form and the user-friendly content update system, which are key user requirements. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_content_workflow_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The user specifically needs a non-technical, easy news-update mechanism. A Supervisor specializing in low-code/no-code content workflows (e.g., S3 drop-zones, Markdown parsing Lambdas, or headless CMS integration) will craft a deterministic process that aligns frontend UX with backend automation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – Content Management Workflow\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne, while well-intentioned, creates a significant overlap in responsibilities with the team under Director Vader.\\n\\nI specifically tasked Director Vader's team, via the \\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content,\\\" with planning the backend mechanics of the simple news/update system (e.g., the S3-triggered Lambda). I tasked Director Vorne's team with designing the *user experience* for this process.\\n\\nRecruiting a \\\"Supervisor – Content Management Workflow\\\" who is responsible for both the frontend UX and backend automation would blur these clearly delineated responsibilities. It is more efficient for the already-approved \\\"Supervisor – User Experience & Sitemap\\\" (under Vorne) and \\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content\\\" (under Vader) to collaborate on this feature. This ensures clear ownership of the frontend and backend components respectively.\\n\\nTherefore, I deny this request to avoid redundancy and maintain a clear separation of concerns within the team structure.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Sloane (4) is requesting approval for call ID SLOANE_RECRUIT_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly plan the contact form mechanism with API Gateway, Lambda, and SES integration, I need an Attendant who specializes in serverless API development and email services\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contact Form API Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a reasonable request for delegation from Supervisor Sloane. Planning the specific integration of API Gateway, Lambda, and SES for the contact form requires focused attention. Assigning an Attendant to this task will ensure a detailed and well-thought-out plan for this feature. The request aligns with the hierarchical structure and promotes efficient task management. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent E (5) is requesting approval for call ID E_RECRUIT_AUTH_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly architect and plan the AWS Cognito authentication system for resident access, I need a dedicated Attendant-rank agent who specializes in identity management and authentication services. This agent will focus exclusively on designing the User Pool configuration, authentication flows, and integration patterns.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication Systems Architect\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a reasonable and well-justified request for delegation. Supervisor E (5), the Supervisor of Identity and Data Security, requires a subordinate to focus on the detailed planning of the AWS Cognito implementation. This is a specialized task that warrants a dedicated agent. Approving this will ensure a thorough and well-architected authentication solution.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Sloane (4) is requesting approval for call ID SLOANE_RECRUIT_002 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the S3-triggered content management system for non-technical users, I need an Attendant who specializes in event-driven architectures and content processing\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Content Management System Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a logical and necessary delegation from Supervisor Sloane. The S3-triggered content system is a core feature for the user, and having a dedicated specialist plan the event-driven architecture will ensure it is designed effectively and robustly. This aligns with the overall goal of creating a simple, non-technical update process. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"This is a logical and necessary delegation from Supervisor Sloane. The S3-triggered content system is a core feature for the user, and having a dedicated specialist plan the event-driven architecture will ensure it is designed effectively and robustly. This aligns with the overall goal of creating a simple, non-technical update process. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":8657,\"candidatesTokenCount\":75,\"totalTokenCount\":8732,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":8092,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8657}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8092}]},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"ftt-aPCqFvPmjMcPtLrQuA8\"},\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":39145,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":382,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":8657,\"outputTokens\":75,\"totalTokens\":8732,\"cachedContentTokens\":8092},\"latencyMs\":2164.3918330000015}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"27e5bf2f565898ac":{"spanId":"27e5bf2f565898ac","traceId":"f7480f0d9639b26ef95721302ecbac83","startTime":1753144188163,"endTime":1753144190330.5625,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit futher down the chain of command and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or a designated Director) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Greetings. I am online and ready to begin operations. My first action will be to greet the user, introduce myself and the firm's capabilities, and gather the initial requirements for our first project. I will use a `CLARIFY` call to accomplish this, as per my instructions. This will allow me to understand the user's vision and begin formulating a plan. I will await the user's response before taking further action, such as recruiting subordinate agents.\\n\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself as the Chief of Staff for your AWS development firm and to gather the foundational requirements of your project. Understanding your vision is the first step in building a successful application.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\",\\n        \\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\",\\n        \\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        [],\\n        [\\n            \\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\",\\n            \\\"An internal business application (e.g., dashboard, CRM, data management tool).\\\",\\n            \\\"A data processing pipeline or backend service.\\\",\\n            \\\"A mobile application backend.\\\",\\n            \\\"Other (please specify).\\\"\\n        ],\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The user's requirements are clear. They need a website for their HOA with both public and restricted sections, user authentication for residents, and a simple content management system for news updates that doesn't require technical skills. This project can be logically divided into two main components: the backend infrastructure and the frontend user experience.\\n\\nTo effectively manage the planning of these components, I will recruit two Director-level agents, each specializing in one of these areas. This will ensure that both the technical foundation and the user-facing aspects of the project are given expert attention from the outset.\\n\\nFirst, I will recruit a Director of Backend Engineering to handle the server-side architecture. Second, I will recruit a Director of Frontend & User Experience to design the website and ensure it meets the user's requirement for simplicity and ease of use. Once these agents are in place, I will issue orders for them to begin creating their respective plans.\\n\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires significant backend infrastructure for user authentication (residents-only access), secure storage of sensitive documents, a contact form mechanism, and the logic for a simplified content management system. A dedicated Director is necessary to architect a robust, secure, and scalable backend solution using the appropriate AWS services.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly requested a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate website. A Director focused on Frontend and User Experience is critical to plan the website structure, design an intuitive interface, and ensure the client-side application is accessible and meets the user's non-technical requirements for content updates.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend & User Experience\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vorne (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"With the successful recruitment of the Director of Backend Engineering (Vader, 3) and the Director of Frontend & User Experience (Vorne, 2), the next logical step is to delegate the initial planning phase to them. I will issue specific orders to each Director, outlining their responsibilities and expected deliverables. These initial plans will form the basis of our comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vader. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the backend infrastructure of the HOA website project. The user requires user authentication for residents, secure storage and access for sensitive documents, a contact form, and a simple mechanism for a non-technical user to post news/updates. Your plan should detail the proposed AWS services (e.g., Cognito, S3, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Lambda, SES) and the high-level architecture for implementing these features. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vorne. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the frontend and user experience of the HOA website project. The user has emphasized the need for a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface. Your plan should cover the website structure (sitemap), hosting strategy (e.g., S3 static hosting with CloudFront), and the user flow for both public visitors and authenticated residents. Crucially, your plan must include a design for the non-technical news update process from a user-experience perspective, ensuring it aligns with the backend capabilities. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_FRONTEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_frontend_infra_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a well-architected, cost-efficient, and secure hosting plan (S3 static hosting, CloudFront distribution, TLS certificates, caching rules, error handling, and deployment pipeline) we need a dedicated senior Supervisor-rank specialist who can dive deep into AWS frontend infrastructure best practices while coordinating with backend counterparts.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – Frontend Infrastructure\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is logical and necessary for developing a robust frontend infrastructure plan. A specialist in this area will ensure that the website is secure, performant, and reliable, which aligns perfectly with the overall project goals. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (3) is requesting approval for call ID vader-recruit-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the Chief's order (HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01), I require a supervisor to oversee the planning of the authentication and secure data storage components. This agent will be responsible for devising the architecture for resident authentication using AWS Cognito and the secure storage and access control mechanisms for sensitive documents, likely utilizing S3 and IAM policies. This is a critical and specialized area of the plan.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Identity and Data Security\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vader is a logical and necessary step to address the critical security requirements of the project. The specialization of a supervisor for identity and data security is a prudent decision that directly supports the successful completion of order `HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01`. I approve this action.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_ux_sitemap_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A seasoned Supervisor focused on user-experience and information architecture is required to design a clear sitemap, page layouts, accessibility considerations, and resident/public user flows that meet the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"simple, user-friendly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" mandate and integrate smoothly with Cognito-based auth and backend APIs.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – User Experience & Sitemap\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is well-justified. The user explicitly requested a \\\"simple and user-friendly interface.\\\" Dedicating a Supervisor to User Experience & Sitemap is a direct and effective way to ensure this core requirement is met. This role is essential for planning the website's structure and user flow, which is a key part of the frontend plan I ordered. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (3) is requesting approval for call ID vader-recruit-02 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the Chief's order (HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01), I require a supervisor to plan the application logic and content management backend. This agent's responsibility will be to design the architecture for the contact form functionality (using services like API Gateway, Lambda, and SES) and the simple news/update system for non-technical users (likely an S3-triggered Lambda process). This will ensure the interactive elements of the backend are well-designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is another well-reasoned request from Director Vader. Separating the planning of application logic from identity and security allows for focused expertise on each component of the backend. This supervisor will be essential for designing the interactive parts of the website, such as the contact form and the user-friendly content update system, which are key user requirements. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_content_workflow_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The user specifically needs a non-technical, easy news-update mechanism. A Supervisor specializing in low-code/no-code content workflows (e.g., S3 drop-zones, Markdown parsing Lambdas, or headless CMS integration) will craft a deterministic process that aligns frontend UX with backend automation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – Content Management Workflow\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne, while well-intentioned, creates a significant overlap in responsibilities with the team under Director Vader.\\n\\nI specifically tasked Director Vader's team, via the \\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content,\\\" with planning the backend mechanics of the simple news/update system (e.g., the S3-triggered Lambda). I tasked Director Vorne's team with designing the *user experience* for this process.\\n\\nRecruiting a \\\"Supervisor – Content Management Workflow\\\" who is responsible for both the frontend UX and backend automation would blur these clearly delineated responsibilities. It is more efficient for the already-approved \\\"Supervisor – User Experience & Sitemap\\\" (under Vorne) and \\\"Supervisor of Application Logic and Content\\\" (under Vader) to collaborate on this feature. This ensures clear ownership of the frontend and backend components respectively.\\n\\nTherefore, I deny this request to avoid redundancy and maintain a clear separation of concerns within the team structure.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Sloane (4) is requesting approval for call ID SLOANE_RECRUIT_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly plan the contact form mechanism with API Gateway, Lambda, and SES integration, I need an Attendant who specializes in serverless API development and email services\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contact Form API Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a reasonable request for delegation from Supervisor Sloane. Planning the specific integration of API Gateway, Lambda, and SES for the contact form requires focused attention. Assigning an Attendant to this task will ensure a detailed and well-thought-out plan for this feature. The request aligns with the hierarchical structure and promotes efficient task management. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent E (5) is requesting approval for call ID E_RECRUIT_AUTH_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly architect and plan the AWS Cognito authentication system for resident access, I need a dedicated Attendant-rank agent who specializes in identity management and authentication services. This agent will focus exclusively on designing the User Pool configuration, authentication flows, and integration patterns.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication Systems Architect\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a reasonable and well-justified request for delegation. Supervisor E (5), the Supervisor of Identity and Data Security, requires a subordinate to focus on the detailed planning of the AWS Cognito implementation. This is a specialized task that warrants a dedicated agent. Approving this will ensure a thorough and well-architected authentication solution.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Sloane (4) is requesting approval for call ID SLOANE_RECRUIT_002 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the S3-triggered content management system for non-technical users, I need an Attendant who specializes in event-driven architectures and content processing\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Content Management System Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is a logical and necessary delegation from Supervisor Sloane. The S3-triggered content system is a core feature for the user, and having a dedicated specialist plan the event-driven architecture will ensure it is designed effectively and robustly. This aligns with the overall goal of creating a simple, non-technical update process. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":39145,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":382,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":8657,\"outputTokens\":75,\"totalTokens\":8732,\"cachedContentTokens\":8092},\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"This is a logical and necessary delegation from Supervisor Sloane. The S3-triggered content system is a core feature for the user, and having a dedicated specialist plan the event-driven architecture will ensure it is designed effectively and robustly. This aligns with the overall goal of creating a simple, non-technical update process. I approve this recruitment.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":8657,\"candidatesTokenCount\":75,\"totalTokenCount\":8732,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":8092,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8657}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":8092}]},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"ftt-aPCqFvPmjMcPtLrQuA8\"},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit futher down the chain of command and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or a designated Director) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Greetings. I am online and ready to begin operations. My first action will be to greet the user, introduce myself and the firm's capabilities, and gather the initial requirements for our first project. I will use a `CLARIFY` call to accomplish this, as per my instructions. This will allow me to understand the user's vision and begin formulating a plan. I will await the user's response before taking further action, such as recruiting subordinate agents.\\n\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself as the Chief of Staff for your AWS development firm and to gather the foundational requirements of your project. Understanding your vision is the first step in building a successful application.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\",\\n        \\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\",\\n        \\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        [],\\n        [\\n            \\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\",\\n            \\\"An internal business application (e.g., dashboard, CRM, data management tool).\\\",\\n            \\\"A data processing pipeline or backend service.\\\",\\n            \\\"A mobile application backend.\\\",\\n            \\\"Other (please specify).\\\"\\n        ],\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T120000Z_CLARIFY_INIT>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Greetings. I am the Chief of Staff, the lead agent of your dedicated AWS software development firm. My purpose is to translate your vision into a fully functional application built entirely within the AWS ecosystem. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you envision building?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What is the primary goal of your project? Please select the option that best describes your objective, or provide your own.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A public-facing website (e.g., blog, marketing site, portfolio).\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Are there any specific technologies or high-level features you have in mind (e.g., user logins, data analytics, a public website, a mobile backend, etc.)? If not, feel free to leave this blank.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:25:53.217Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The user's requirements are clear. They need a website for their HOA with both public and restricted sections, user authentication for residents, and a simple content management system for news updates that doesn't require technical skills. This project can be logically divided into two main components: the backend infrastructure and the frontend user experience.\\n\\nTo effectively manage the planning of these components, I will recruit two Director-level agents, each specializing in one of these areas. This will ensure that both the technical foundation and the user-facing aspects of the project are given expert attention from the outset.\\n\\nFirst, I will recruit a Director of Backend Engineering to handle the server-side architecture. Second, I will recruit a Director of Frontend & User Experience to design the website and ensure it meets the user's requirement for simplicity and ease of use. Once these agents are in place, I will issue orders for them to begin creating their respective plans.\\n\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project requires significant backend infrastructure for user authentication (residents-only access), secure storage of sensitive documents, a contact form mechanism, and the logic for a simplified content management system. A dedicated Director is necessary to architect a robust, secure, and scalable backend solution using the appropriate AWS services.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user has explicitly requested a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate website. A Director focused on Frontend and User Experience is critical to plan the website structure, design an intuitive interface, and ensure the client-side application is accessible and meets the user's non-technical requirements for content updates.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend & User Experience\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130000Z_RECRUIT_BACKEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240514T130001Z_RECRUIT_FRONTEND>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vorne (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:27:47.279Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"With the successful recruitment of the Director of Backend Engineering (Vader, 3) and the Director of Frontend & User Experience (Vorne, 2), the next logical step is to delegate the initial planning phase to them. I will issue specific orders to each Director, outlining their responsibilities and expected deliverables. These initial plans will form the basis of our comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vader. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the backend infrastructure of the HOA website project. The user requires user authentication for residents, secure storage and access for sensitive documents, a contact form, and a simple mechanism for a non-technical user to post news/updates. Your plan should detail the proposed AWS services (e.g., Cognito, S3, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Lambda, SES) and the high-level architecture for implementing these features. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140000Z_ORDER_BACKEND>###\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Greetings, Director Vorne. Your primary task is to develop a comprehensive plan for the frontend and user experience of the HOA website project. The user has emphasized the need for a simple, user-friendly, and easy-to-navigate interface. Your plan should cover the website structure (sitemap), hosting strategy (e.g., S3 static hosting with CloudFront), and the user flow for both public visitors and authenticated residents. Crucially, your plan must include a design for the non-technical news update process from a user-experience perspective, ensuring it aligns with the backend capabilities. This plan will be a critical component of the final project DEP. Please recruit any necessary subordinate agents to assist you and report back with your completed plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"HOA_PLAN_FRONTEND_01\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240514T140001Z_ORDER_FRONTEND>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_frontend_infra_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a well-architected, cost-efficient, and secure hosting plan (S3 static hosting, CloudFront distribution, TLS certificates, caching rules, error handling, and deployment pipeline) we need a dedicated senior Supervisor-rank specialist who can dive deep into AWS frontend infrastructure best practices while coordinating with backend counterparts.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – Frontend Infrastructure\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is logical and necessary for developing a robust frontend infrastructure plan. A specialist in this area will ensure that the website is secure, performant, and reliable, which aligns perfectly with the overall project goals. I approve this request.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vader (3) is requesting approval for call ID vader-recruit-01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To fulfill the Chief's order (HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01), I require a supervisor to oversee the planning of the authentication and secure data storage components. This agent will be responsible for devising the architecture for resident authentication using AWS Cognito and the secure storage and access control mechanisms for sensitive documents, likely utilizing S3 and IAM policies. This is a critical and specialized area of the plan.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor of Identity and Data Security\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vader is a logical and necessary step to address the critical security requirements of the project. The specialization of a supervisor for identity and data security is a prudent decision that directly supports the successful completion of order `HOA_PLAN_BACKEND_01`. I approve this action.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vorne (2) is requesting approval for call ID rec_ux_sitemap_01 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A seasoned Supervisor focused on user-experience and information architecture is required to design a clear sitemap, page layouts, accessibility considerations, and resident/public user flows that meet the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"simple, user-friendly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" mandate and integrate smoothly with Cognito-based auth and backend APIs.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Supervisor – User Experience & Sitemap\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This recruitment request from Director Vorne is well-justified. The user explicitly requested a \\\"simple and user-friendly interface.\\\" Dedicating a Supervisor to User Experience & Sitemap is a direct and effective way to ensure this core requirement is met. This role is essential 